  "about": "Round 21: how a vocal side is led. estribillo = rhythm-led: the orchestra carries the side and the singer (an estribillista) comes in later for a refrain; cantor = singer-led: the singer (a cantor de orquesta) sings the lyric and leads the side. Matched by orchestra id + singer surname (+ recording years). A side no rule names and recorded after 1936 is unknown and never constrains a tanda; a vocal side up to 1936 is estribillo (the refrain era). A DJ's correction in the database wins. Sources: the standard orchestra histories (Lefcovich discographies, todotango.com singer biographies, the golden-age review docs/reviews/round13-best-years.md); a heuristic for the 1935-45 canon, not a per-side listening.",
